WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.150
Two more kinds of evidence
sit beside the drift.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:07.761
The review cycle reads the review
records that Chapters 7 and 9 build;

3
00:00:07.761 --> 00:00:11.725
this chapter doesn't run the
reviews, it reads their records.

4
00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:14.158
Following the program's design guidance,

5
00:00:14.158 --> 00:00:17.879
it flags an app holding Graph
permissions whose owners haven't

6
00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:21.600
reviewed it in ninety-two days,
and agent access with no end date.

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.568
And it flags an agent with no
sponsor attestation in a year;

8
00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:30.775
Microsoft Learn's best practices for
Agent I D say every six to twelve months.

9
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:34.256
And a kind of review record that
never arrived is a warning,

10
00:00:34.256 --> 00:00:37.012
because a missing record
isn't a passed review.

11
00:00:37.012 --> 00:00:41.153
Then once a year, the program's
vintage comparison checks this

12
00:00:41.153 --> 00:00:45.050
year's A I use-case inventory
against last year's, by use case.

13
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.729
It catches a new piloted or
deployed system with no identity,

14
00:00:48.729 --> 00:00:53.731
a retired one whose identities are still
enabled, a changed authorization answer,

15
00:00:53.731 --> 00:00:57.980
and an entry that left the inventory
without being reported retired.
